{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/39036909?","display_login":"gattsuru","gravatar_id":"","id":"39036909","login":"gattsuru","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:32Z","id":"14690747026","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/5167336?","gravatar_id":"","id":"5167336","login":"ldtteam","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/ldtteam"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"> How far along is this?\\r\\n\\r\\nThe data-side functionality is set, I think everyone\'s had a pretty good swing at the json format and approach, and it\'s has tested to be robust in both single-player and dedicated server modes.  \\r\\n\\r\\nPresentation\\/UI side, ShadowProtocol gave a lot of good advice in the last couple days, and that\'s the majority of the last push. (My apologies for turning the new-features-showoff channel into a UI\\/UX club). I think it\'s come together pretty well, but it did involve a significant change, so I don\'t know if it needs Nightenom to look over it. That\'s not _done_, but I think anything remaining is going to be small tweaks to textures or button shapes that can wait for another PR.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe only potential large matter is the individualized research icons.  For now, they\'re disabled, but I\'ve left the code and the json attributes there to have them show up only for completed research.  Toggling ResearchConstants#DRAW_ICONS to true will turn it back on if anyone wants to try them -- enabled, it draws the icons from the json files for completed research; otherwise, it leaves a green check.  We can push as-is, or I can get rid of the Research \\"icon\\" tag and reinsert down the road if we ever get them looking nice.\\r\\n\\r\\nHowever, the current committed version is dependent on https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ldtteam\\/Structurize\\/pull\\/239 .  I\'ve got a fallback version if we can\'t go to the new tooltips code, but it would be a separate commit and push, and it only really covers the effects.","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:31Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/pull\\/6181#issuecomment-753495381","id":"753495381","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/issues\\/6181","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTM4MQ==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:31Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495381","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars1.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/39036909?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/gattsuru","id":"39036909","login":"gattsuru","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDM2OTA5","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/gattsuru"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Closes #6178 \\r\\nCloses #6300 \\r\\nCloses #5027\\r\\n\\r\\n# Changes proposed in this pull request:\\r\\n- Moves all research from static assignment in ResearchInitializer to a json-based data pack.  Hardens inputs to handle most possible inconsistent behaviors from malformed user data packs, as well as moving forward past saves where the research names were spelled differently.\\r\\n- Moves any research effect-related constants possible out of coremod and into com.minecolonies.api.research.util\'s ResearchConstants.java.\\r\\n- Compresses the various ResearchEffect types into a single GlobalResearchEffect, of type double.  Adds functionality so that building upgrades can now be locked by research, if the research effect has levels defined.\\r\\n- Fixes a number of research-related small bugs; tooltips a la #6300 , saturation-limit research having a flipped sign.\\r\\n- Removes the individual blockhut-based research unlocks behaviors and compresses to AbstractBlockHut; if there\'s no research effect with the correct name, they\'ll be allowed, if there is and it isn\'t complete, they\'ll show the error tooltip and not be able to build.  Blockhut research can also now have levels, in which case, the hut can only be upgraded to the unlocked level.\\r\\n- Adds sounds for research-related successes and failures.\\r\\n- Removes research costs from server config file, as they\'re now handled in data packs.\\r\\n- Reworks the WindowUniversityHut and WindowResearchTree windows, adding tooltips, icons, and tightening up the UI.  Adds a cancel and reset button for in-progess and completed research respectively.\\r\\n- Cancelling completed research has a cost, and that cost is configurable through the config file.\\r\\n- Adds some debugging research-related settings to server config file, and logging to both dynamic and static loading of researches.\\r\\n- Adds serialization and deserialization to properly synch data packs from the server to clients in a dedicated server environment.  This message is only sent on initial connection, and when the server executes a data pack reload.\\r\\n\\r\\nResearch datapacks must be placed into the minecolonies\\/researches directory, and can consist of :\\r\\n- research-jsons, which require the \\"id\\":string (used as identifier and to autogenerate translation keys), \\"branch\\":, \\"requiredUniversityLevel\\":int, and may optionally have \\"subtitle\\":string,  \\"icon\\":string (which must match an item or existing texture file resource location, or falls back to air blocks), \\"parentResearch\\":string (using the parent research\'s id), \\"requirements\\":array-of-objects, and \\"effects\\":array-of-objects.\\r\\n- Research without an effect can still cause recipes to be unlocked, since the recipe json side works off research ids.\\r\\n- research-effect-jsons, which require the \\"id\\" and \\"effect\\": true properties.  Effects can also have optional \\"subtitle\\":string and \\"level\\":array-of-numbers fields.  Effects without a \\"level\\" property are assumed to go from 0.0 to 5.0 when triggered (basically, hut unlocks).\\r\\n- optional research-remove jsons, which must contain \\"remove\\":boolean and \\"id\\":string tags.  They remove researches, if the research with the matching ID is present.\\r\\n- optional branch jsons, which must contain \\"branch-id\\".  These can be used to set with the \\"base-time\\":double modifier which is multiplied to the normal time required for a specific research on that branch, and\\/or to give a different name to the branch in the University Hut interface through the \\"name\\":string property (which must be the displayed text or a full translation key).\\r\\n\\r\\nReview please\\r\\n","comments":"11","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/issues\\/6181\\/comments","created_at":"2020-12-02T03:08:28Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/issues\\/6181\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/pull\\/6181","id":"754894352","labels":[],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/issues\\/6181\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NTMwNzA5NzAx","number":"6181","pull_request":{"diff_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ldtteam\\/minecolonies\\/pull\\