{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/41823704?","display_login":"Kafoo","gravatar_id":"","id":"41823704","login":"Kafoo","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/Kafoo"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:43Z","id":"14690747785","payload":{"before":"d2dfe112072b9be4cb71c591b9634e0ccc6e431f","commits":[{"author":{"email":"bb9dc3dcbb16337aa76ea44e5705229b65e4c41a@gmail.com","name":"Antoine"},"distinct":true,"message":"minupdate","sha":"aafa6f1531adcfcf2e32374f9639664e19703d5b","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/Kafoo\\/sitko_back\\/commits\\/aafa6f1531adcfcf2e32374f9639664e19703d5b"}],"distinct_size":"1","head":"aafa6f1531adcfcf2e32374f9639664e19703d5b","push_id":"6285846653","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/main","size":"1"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"310000354","name":"Kafoo\\/sitko_back","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/Kafoo\\/sitko_back"},"type":"PushEvent"}
{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/20465600?","display_login":"ngreifer","gravatar_id":"","id":"20465600","login":"ngreifer","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:43Z","id":"14690747787","payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"OWNER","body":"Thank you so much for letting me know about this! It should e fixed now.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe problem was due to `WegithIt` splitting the `race` factor variable into three categories and supplying all of them to `CBPS()`, which meant the design matrix was not full rank, leading to erratic behavior. You can actually replicate this using `CBPS()` in the following way:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nlalonde_split <- cobalt::splitfactor(lalonde, drop.first = FALSE)\\r\\n\\r\\nps_1 <- CBPS(\\r\\n  treat ~ age + educ + race_black + race_hispan + race_white + married + nodegree + re74 + re75,\\r\\n  data = lalonde_split, ATT = 0\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nps_2 <- CBPS(\\r\\n  treat ~ educ + race_black + race_hispan + race_white + nodegree + re74 + re75 + married + age,\\r\\n  data = lalonde_split, ATT = 0\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nhead(data.frame(\\r\\n  ps1 = ps_1$fitted.values,\\r\\n  ps2 = ps_2$fitted.values\\r\\n))\\r\\n```\\r\\nI\'ve fixed `weightit()` so that it ensures the matrix is full rank, yielding the same propensity scores every time.","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:43Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ngreifer\\/WeightIt\\/issues\\/16#issuecomment-753495427","id":"753495427","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ngreifer\\/WeightIt\\/issues\\/16","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTQyNw==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:37:43Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ngreifer\\/WeightIt\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495427","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars1.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/20465600?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ngreifer","id":"20465600","login":"ngreifer","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNDY1NjAw","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ngreifer"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"Hi!\\r\\n\\r\\nThanks for the great package!\\r\\n\\r\\nI have noticed that when `method = \\"cbps\\"` is used in the `weightit` function different PSs values are returned if the covariates on the right-hand side of the formula are specified in different orders. However, if PSs are estimated \\"outside\\" of the `weightit` function using `CBPS::CBPS` they look identical. Here\'s a reproducible example using `lalonde` dataset.\\r\\n\\r\\n``` r\\r\\nlibrary(WeightIt)\\r\\nlibrary(CBPS)\\r\\n#> Loading required package: MASS\\r\\n#> Loading required package: MatchIt\\r\\n#> Loading required package: nnet\\r\\n#> Loading required package: numDeriv\\r\\n#> Loading required package: glmnet\\r\\n#> Loading required package: Matrix\\r\\n#> Loaded glmnet 4.0-2\\r\\n#> CBPS: Covariate Balancing Propensity Score\\r\\n#> Version: 0.21\\r\\n#> Authors: Christian Fong [aut, cre],\\r\\n#>   Marc Ratkovic [aut],\\r\\n#>   Kosuke Imai [aut],\\r\\n#>   Chad Hazlett [ctb],\\r\\n#>   Xiaolin Yang [ctb],\\r\\n#>   Sida Peng [ctb]\\r\\n\\r\\ndata(\\"lalonde\\")\\r\\n\\r\\n# 1) PS estimation using CBPS function ---------------------------------\\r\\nps_1 <- CBPS(\\r\\n  treat ~ age + educ + race + married + nodegree + re74 + re75,\\r\\n  data = lalonde, ATT = 0\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nps_2 <- CBPS(\\r\\n  treat ~ educ + race + nodegree + re74 + re75 + married + age,\\r\\n  data = lalonde, ATT = 0\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nhead(data.frame(\\r\\n  ps1 = ps_1$fitted.values,\\r\\n  ps2 = ps_2$fitted.values\\r\\n))\\r\\n#>         ps1       ps2\\r\\n#> 1 0.6283220 0.6283220\\r\\n#> 2 0.2217905 0.2217905\\r\\n#> 3 0.6629598 0.6629598\\r\\n#> 4 0.7595289 0.7595289\\r\\n#> 5 0.6939144 0.6939144\\r\\n#> 6 0.6906981 0.6906981\\r\\n\\r\\n# The PSs are identical\\r\\n\\r\\n# 2) PS estimation using weightit --------------------------------------\\r\\nwt_1 <- weightit(\\r\\n  treat ~ age + educ + race + married + nodegree + re74 + re75,\\r\\n  data = lalonde,\\r\\n  method = \\"cbps\\",\\r\\n  estimand = \\"ATE\\"\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nwt_2 <- weightit(\\r\\n  treat ~ educ + race + nodegree + re74 + re75 + married + age,\\r\\n  data = lalonde,\\r\\n  method = \\"cbps\\",\\r\\n  estimand = \\"ATE\\"\\r\\n)\\r\\n\\r\\nhead(data.frame(\\r\\n  ps1 = wt_1$ps,\\r\\n  ps2 = wt_2$ps\\r\\n))\\r\\n#>         ps1       ps2\\r\\n#> 1 0.6897437 0.5851259\\r\\n#> 2 0.2157126 0.2275898\\r\\n#> 3 0.6599305 0.7606147\\r\\n#> 4 0.7763387 0.7580954\\r\\n#> 5 0.6329184 0.6942782\\r\\n#> 6 0.6930129 0.6907725\\r\\n\\r\\n# The PSs are not identical\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n<sup>Created on 2020-12-28 by the [reprex package](https:\\/\\/reprex.tidyverse.org) (v0.3.0)<\\/sup>\\r\\n\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n\\r\\n<summary>Session info<\\/summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n``` r\\r\\ndevtools::session_info()\\r\\n#> - Session info ---------------------------------------------------------------\\r\\n#>  setting  value                       \\r\\n#>  version  R version 4.0.3 (2020-10-10)\\r\\n#>  os       Windows 10 x64              \\r\\n#>  system   x86_64, mingw32             \\r\\n#>  ui       RTerm                       \\r\\n#>  language (EN)             