mail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Recycle CDC transfer descriptors\\n\\nDon\'t block and fail when all transfers are active. Instead,\\nrecycle all of the other non-current TDs.\\n\\nBy not recycling the current TD, we leave stale data in the\\ntransfer queue. This is a won\'t-fix issue; it should be considered\\nwhen writing a Rust-based USB driver.","sha":"6ad05e8169c6ca1e00f6084d18e1813ccd5c16e2","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/6ad05e8169c6ca1e00f6084d18e1813ccd5c16e2"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Add additional usb::Writer::flush docs","sha":"b70293fd4d8ebcefdf574d79e3c82c8d702f004c","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/b70293fd4d8ebcefdf574d79e3c82c8d702f004c"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Remove systick requirement from USB interface\\n\\nUpdate examples, docs, and tests","sha":"e599b2d86bc26be1367a18629ef0c4ca26a9abd5","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/e599b2d86bc26be1367a18629ef0c4ca26a9abd5"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Decouple usb-logging and systick features\\n\\nRemove caveat from BSP docs","sha":"beb960d243958da4e0a9e93f32b6e58b18e64ecd","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/beb960d243958da4e0a9e93f32b6e58b18e64ecd"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Conditionally copy the libt4usb library\\n\\nWe only link against it if the feature is enabled. We can skip\\nthe copy if we don\'t need it.","sha":"b9ff189c1b8117d5770ac4de6cdf04ce4484a286","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/b9ff189c1b8117d5770ac4de6cdf04ce4484a286"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Merge branch \'rtic-example-usb\' of https:\\/\\/github.com\\/mitchmindtree\\/teensy4-rs into mitchmindtree-rtic-example-usb","sha":"f7dee57e669a9e38725e486f8367f70a41e666fc","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/f7dee57e669a9e38725e486f8367f70a41e666fc"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Update CHANGELOG","sha":"c71d676d83ec9a61496a49f271a0c478252f764a","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/c71d676d83ec9a61496a49f271a0c478252f764a"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Add USB polling status","sha":"baa3060dc4723fb86fd3bdd83db422418649ec67","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commits\\/baa3060dc4723fb86fd3bdd83db422418649ec67"},{"author":{"email":"8933ddf7b87afa7adc46eb44f50d893d30a43e8b@gmail.com","name":"Ian McIntyre"},"distinct":false,"message":"Move USB_OTG1 ISRs into examples\\n\\nAfter this commit, users are required to call usb::poll() themselves.\\nWe recommend that they do this by defining the USB_OTG1 interrupt\\nhandler, and calling the poll() method in the implementation. The docs\\nguide users towards the ISR approach.\\n\\nThe change supports advanced USB usage in RTIC. An RTIC user can now\\nimplement the ISR, and check the poll status to see if there\'s data\\nfrom the host. Without this kind of change, the user would need to\\npoll the reader on an interval. Users can still do this, but now they\\ncan schedule a \\"read from USB\\" task as necessary.","sha":"008e42a1ab2a4b002c9b90b2ecb3df7c8b72002b","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/mciantyre\\/teensy4-rs\\/commit