{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/367900?","display_login":"bcbnz","gravatar_id":"","id":"367900","login":"bcbnz","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bcbnz"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:05Z","id":"14690749142","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/17927519?","gravatar_id":"","id":"17927519","login":"jupyterhub","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/jupyterhub"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"NONE","body":"I think doing this opens up some security issues, at least without further configuration. As the single-user server is now running with CAP_SETUID, any code run in a notebook or terminal can set the UID to 0 and run any further code as root:\\r\\n\\r\\n```Jupyter Notebook\\r\\n [In 1]: import os\\r\\n         os.setuid(0)\\r\\n\\r\\n [In 2]: os.getuid()\\r\\n[Out 2]: 0\\r\\n\\r\\n [In 3]: import subprocess\\r\\n         subprocess.run(\\"whoami\\", capture_output=True).stdout\\r\\n[Out 3]: b\'root\\\\n\'\\r\\n```","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:05Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/jupyterhub\\/sudospawner\\/issues\\/62#issuecomment-753495484","id":"753495484","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jupyterhub\\/sudospawner\\/issues\\/62","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTQ4NA==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:05Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jupyterhub\\/sudospawner\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495484","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars0.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/367900?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bcbnz\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bcbnz\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bcbnz\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bcbnz\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/bcbnz","id":"367900","login":"bcbnz","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NzkwMA==",