{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/5637090?","display_login":"ruscur","gravatar_id":"","id":"5637090","login":"ruscur","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ruscur"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:16Z","id":"14690749821","payload":{"before":"26602f8a06e49427f8e4403dce5238d9eae17cf8","commits":[{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: rewrite idle synchronisation\\n\\nThis changes CPU idle synchronisation to always kick all other CPUs\\nout of idle code first whenever idle settings (pm_enabled, IPIs, sreset\\netc) are to be changed.\\n\\nCurrently this is somewhat racy and not obviously correct, with\\npm_enabled changing while in low level idle routines, which does\\nresult in messages like \\"cpu_idle_p9 called pm disabled\\".\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"cdb0d68765528667dbf4f82ee3c5774d3babf77c","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/cdb0d68765528667dbf4f82ee3c5774d3babf77c"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: remove POWER8 IPI loop\\n\\nPOWER8 should not have to loop sending IPIs until the destination\\nwakes up. One should be enough.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"319938bc837e518c39ad8c1f53542ee974e2defe","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/319938bc837e518c39ad8c1f53542ee974e2defe"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: refactor IPI sending\\n\\nPull the IPI sending code into its own function where it is used in\\ntwo places.\\n\\ncpu_wake() already checks in_idle, so its caller does not need to\\ncheck pm_enabled.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"af36b90318cabce244205f7de37874da44f139b4","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/af36b90318cabce244205f7de37874da44f139b4"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: move cpu_wake out of job_lock, only wake if necessary\\n\\nThere is no need to keep the IPI initiation under the job_lock.\\nIf the target does wake after the job is queued and before we can\\nsend the IPI, it will check for new jobs.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"257f2e151dd9c9b7b9b924e8465657f487881c88","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/257f2e151dd9c9b7b9b924e8465657f487881c88"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: make cpu idle states simpler\\n\\nin_idle is true for any kind of idle. This is not used anywhere\\nexcept for state assertions, but it could be used to remove the\\nidle_lock and global counter if that becomes a significant\\ncost.\\n\\nin_sleep is true for sleep that requires an IPI to wake up.\\n\\nin_job_sleep is true for sleep that wants an IPI sent after a job is\\nqueued, and implies in_sleep.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"118ad05ba82898e04182abb2541bfa48e37fdeca","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/118ad05ba82898e04182abb2541bfa48e37fdeca"}],"distinct_size":"5","head":"118ad05ba82898e04182abb2541bfa48e37fdeca","push_id":"6285848042","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/_5_6__core_cpu__make_cpu_idle_states_simpler_mbox_master","size":"5"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"52412231","name":"ruscur\\/skiboot","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot"},"type":"PushEvent"}
