{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/3660?","display_login":"demonnic","gravatar_id":"","id":"3660","login":"demonnic","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:54Z","id":"14690752140","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/19184012?","gravatar_id":"","id":"19184012","login":"IRE-Mudlet-Mapping","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"NONE","body":"I mean personally, I\'d prefer promptmove be the default action and it not need to be an option, but it\'s technically slower and I thought it might be preferred to keep as much of the current behaviour as possible, for most people they\'ll never even notice this was changed. But promptmove solves the number one complaint I\'ve seen from people about the mapper, so I\'m not sure I agree that it is a niche usecase. \\r\\n\\r\\nI can just set promptmove to use the slowwalk setting if that\'s the only way you\'ll take the change though. I don\'t mind using both at once and can just submit fixes for the times the command spamming are pasting over failed or forced movement since I won\'t be able to have that fallback timer anymore.","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:54Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pull\\/137#issuecomment-753495618","id":"753495618","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/137","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTYxOA==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:54Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495618","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars1.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/3660?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/demonnic","id":"3660","login":"demonnic","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjA=","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"## Purpose of change\\r\\n\\r\\nAdd a bit of configurability, and make slowwalk less useless\\r\\nAdd option to use prompt triggers for actual movement, but use Room.Info for the logic (see below)\\r\\n\\r\\nRight now, `mconfig slowwalk on` fails movement any time it hits a too hasty message, needs to open a door, or anything else tries to set a timer for the next movement piece, for any reason.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhereas I feel like it\'s really about not spamming the server with movement commands constantly. I have created a compromise of sorts\\r\\n\\r\\n## More detailed list of changes\\r\\n\\r\\nI\'m sorry that this kind of touches on several things, but they were all kind of related and were tested together.\\r\\n\\r\\n* If you install this version and change nothing, with slowwalk set to false, then the behaviour should be exactly the same as it is now\\r\\n* `mconfig slowwalk on` now prevents the overall failback timer which currently spams the movement command every half second (+previous latency). This is nice for laggy connections, as if you get an 8 second lag spike, you\'ve spammed the command up to 16 times just from that timer\\r\\n  * unlike before, however, slowwalk does not prevent it from attempting to resend the command after a \\"don\'t be too hasty\\" message, or in places where setmovetimer() is being used to try movement again (doors, too hasty messages, other failure conditions)\\r\\n* adds `mconfig promptmove <on\\/off>` option. \\r\\n  * When set to false\\/off, current behaviour is maintained (the mmp.move function call is immediate to the Room.Info event), but when on\\/true it creates a single-fire prompt trigger which fires off the mmp.move call. This delays the movement just long enough to ensure you\'ve received Char.Items.List\\/etc and have had a chance to intelligently decide if you want to pause the mapper for some reason. This aids in accurately stopping for autowalk searching (find the ore, find a mob, whatever). Right now on Lusternia the mapper has decided to move on and done so before Char.Items.List ever pops for you to tell it to hold on.\\r\\n* adds `mconfig fastmovetime <number>` to adjust the time used for the failsafe timer that slowwalk controls still. Defaults to 0.5 still, but can now be adjusted for those with laggy connections who still want that final failsafe. Defaulting to 0.5 should mean no change for anyone who does not explicitly set a new value though.\\r\\n* fixes `mconfig` alias to allow for setting number values and having their types be guarded like string\\/booleans are\\r\\n* adds patterns for doors which were previously missing and causing the mapper to get hung up in Lusternia (but doors are listed in a separate group so put it there)\\r\\n* adds a forced movement pattern I discovered in Lusternia while testing the autowalker with slowwalk on in Serenwilde in Lusternia\\r\\n\\r\\n## Testing done\\r\\n\\r\\nIn none of these games do I really own or use travel artefacts. \\r\\n\\r\\nAlso, there may be cases where stop conditions are not being cleanly handled now but glossed over by the failsafe timer spam. \\r\\n\\r\\nAll were tested with slowwalk and promptmove on\\r\\n\\r\\nThe most testing was done on Lusternia, as it\'s the game I know best and am currently most active in. \\r\\n\\r\\n* Achaea\\r\\n  * Run from Savannah to Cyrene for food, and back to the Savannah. Seemed to work well overall, no accidental stoppages, stopped on all the mobs it was meant to stop on\\r\\n* Lusternia\\r\\n  * extensive testing in and around Serenwilde and some in Gaudiguch. 100% accuracy with stopping.\\r\\n* Aetolia\\r\\n  * Tested with a new character in the tutorial zone. No issues but not exactly extensive either\\r\\n* Imperian\\r\\n  * Tested in... Khandava I think it was? I found an old character. Had issues with doors but they were issues the current mapper has as well\\r\\n* Starmoun\\r\\n  * Tested around Reynolds Station and New Haven. Still moved around properly, did not get caught on using transports or anything like that.","comments":"4","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/137\\/comments","created_at":"2021-01-02T00:30:34Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/137\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pull\\/137","id":"777377858","labels":[],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/137\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NTQ3Njk0NzA4","number":"137","pull_request":{"diff_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pull\\/137.diff","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pull\\/137","patch_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pull\\/137.patch","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/pulls\\/137"},"repository_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script","state":"open","title":"Add some options to make the walker more reliable\\/accurate","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:54Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script\\/issues\\/137","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars1.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/3660?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/demonnic","id":"3660","login":"demonnic","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NjA=","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/demonnic"}}},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"33596713","name":"IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/IRE-Mudlet-Mapping\\/ire-mapping-script"},"type":"IssueCommentEvent"}
