{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/5637090?","display_login":"ruscur","gravatar_id":"","id":"5637090","login":"ruscur","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ruscur"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:56Z","id":"14690752235","payload":{"before":"d60a0d3af75c5c2aa7c54c875fdeb8fbb5eacb9f","commits":[{"author":{"email":"4e2d3d12816ace76f1cfa36c1816509bd24cf089@csgroup.eu","name":"Christophe Leroy"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/32s: Do DABR match out of handle_page_fault()\\n\\nhandle_page_fault() has some code dedicated to book3s\\/32 to\\ncall do_break() when the DSI is a DABR match.\\n\\nOn other platforms, do_break() is handled separately.\\n\\nDo the same for book3s\\/32, do it earlier in the process of DSI.\\n\\nThis change also avoid doing the test on ISI.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Christophe Leroy <christophe.leroy@csgroup.eu>","sha":"1a8e98f65be987581e72421d58cf5aefa34856f9","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/1a8e98f65be987581e72421d58cf5aefa34856f9"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s: move the last of the page fault handling logic to C\\n\\nThe page fault handling still has some complex logic particularly around\\nhash table handling, in asm. Implement this in C instead.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"ac8343e8e9f02712b0d6695e70bbbbb214ec8276","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/ac8343e8e9f02712b0d6695e70bbbbb214ec8276"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: remove arguments from fault handler functions\\n\\nMake mm fault handlers all just take the pt_regs * argument and load\\nDAR\\/DSISR from that. Make those that return a value return long.\\n\\nThis is done to make the function signatures match other handlers, which\\nwill help with a future patch to add wrappers. Explicit arguments could\\nbe added for performance but that would require more wrapper macro\\nvariants.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"4c210296d78ae70c272c0bf41963aa737d90ff35","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/4c210296d78ae70c272c0bf41963aa737d90ff35"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: bad_page_fault, do_break get registers from regs\\n\\nSimilar to the previous patch this makes interrupt handler function\\ntypes more regular so they can be wrapped with the next patch.\\n\\nbad_page_fault and do_break are not performance critical.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"1866ac8cae70e0d7b468b49ff4635edb3d2c60e5","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/1866ac8cae70e0d7b468b49ff4635edb3d2c60e5"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/perf: move perf irq\\/nmi handling details into traps.c\\n\\nThis is required in order to allow more significant differences between\\nNMI type interrupt handlers and regular asynchronous handlers.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"0c638dbcac2ec0f7819831a0f2b260c6ed6a817a","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/0c638dbcac2ec0f7819831a0f2b260c6ed6a817a"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: interrupt handler wrapper functions\\n\\nAdd wrapper functions (derived from x86 macros) for interrupt handler\\nfunctions. This allows interrupt entry code to be written in C.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"40b6fa900044ac2345ed72c90aa841ec549e9310","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/40b6fa900044ac2345ed72c90aa841ec549e9310"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: add interrupt wrapper entry \\/ exit stub functions\\n\\nThese will be used by subsequent patches.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"c521f165e2a5fa736d7b4fd79a510d0dac74322f","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/c521f165e2a5fa736d7b4fd79a510d0dac74322f"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: add interrupt_cond_local_irq_enable helper\\n\\nSimple helper for synchronous interrupt handlers (i.e., process-context)\\nto enable interrupts if it was taken in an interrupts-enabled context.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"4a49646789eefe122a92f1282c8c281e54d2f0a1","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/4a49646789eefe122a92f1282c8c281e54d2f0a1"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64: context tracking remove _TIF_NOHZ\\n\\nAdd context tracking to the system call handler explicitly, and remove\\n_TIF_NOHZ.\\n\\nThis saves 35 cycles on gettid system call cost on POWER9 with a\\nCONFIG_NOHZ_FULL kernel.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"65bd490ded87ecc3840f3957d4fac7ee506f628f","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/65bd490ded87ecc3840f3957d4fac7ee506f628f"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s\\/hash: improve context tracking of hash faults\\n\\nThis moves the 64s\\/hash context tracking from hash_page_mm() to\\n__do_hash_fault(), so it\'s no longer called by OCXL \\/ SPU\\naccelerators, which was certainly the wrong thing to be doing,\\nbecause those callers are not low level interrupt handlers, so\\nshould have entered a kernel context tracking already.\\n\\nThen remain in kernel context for the duration of the fault,\\nrather than enter\\/exit for the hash fault then enter\\/exit for\\nthe page fault, which is pointless.\\n\\nEven still, calling exception_enter\\/exit in __do_hash_fault seems\\nquestionable because that\'s touching per-cpu variables, tracing,\\netc., which might have been interrupted by this hash fault or\\nthemselves cause hash faults. But maybe I miss something because\\nhash_page_mm very deliberately calls trace_hash_fault too, for\\nexample. So for now go with it, it\'s no worse than before, in this\\nregard.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"27c92a28917d1a21658c65bfb01c88290c539064","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/27c92a28917d1a21658c65bfb01c88290c539064"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64: context tracking move to interrupt wrappers\\n\\nThis moves exception_enter\\/exit calls to wrapper functions for\\nsynchronous interrupts. More interrupt handlers are covered by\\nthis than previously.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"e43a3343920041be80734aa24041c0a04b848933","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/e43a3343920041be80734aa24041c0a04b848933"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64: add context tracking to asynchronous interrupts\\n\\nPreviously context tracking was not done for asynchronous interrupts,\\n(those that run in interrupt context), and if those would cause a\\nreschedule when they exit, then scheduling functions (schedule_user,\\npreempt_schedule_irq) call exception_enter\\/exit to fix this up and\\nexit user context.\\n\\nThis is a hack we would like to get away from, so do context tracking\\nfor asynchronous interrupts too.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"58ff62d378134dc7a58ade570f47b85e5d4d24b4","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/58ff62d378134dc7a58ade570f47b85e5d4d24b4"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: handle irq_enter\\/irq_exit in interrupt handler wrappers\\n\\nMove irq_enter\\/irq_exit into asynchronous interrupt handler wrappers.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"27c632886e0a0d3bb0db3221a42be198e54158bc","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/27c632886e0a0d3bb0db3221a42be198e54158bc"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s: move context tracking exit to interrupt exit path\\n\\nThe interrupt handler wrapper functions are not the ideal place to\\nmaintain context tracking because after they return, the low level exit\\ncode must then determine if there are interrupts to replay, or if the\\ntask should be preempted, etc. Those paths (e.g., schedule_user) include\\ntheir own exception_enter\\/exit pairs to fix this up but it\'s a bit hacky\\n(see schedule_user() comments).\\n\\nIdeally context tracking will go to user mode only when there are no\\nmore interrupts or context switches or other exit processing work to\\nhandle.\\n\\n64e can not do this because it does not use the C interrupt exit code.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"1463b0bb57ef88c3f9497e02c3d4a24a71571146","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/1463b0bb57ef88c3f9497e02c3d4a24a71571146"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s: reconcile interrupts in C\\n\\nThere is no need for this to be in asm, use the new intrrupt entry wrapper.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"661535908d73338e92d092814a9e2a3896bb8f8b","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/661535908d73338e92d092814a9e2a3896bb8f8b"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64: move account_stolen_time into its own function\\n\\nThis will be used by interrupt entry as well.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"f3da4f3533301c4337f2d6f126374dce033a41f3","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/f3da4f3533301c4337f2d6f126374dce033a41f3"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64: entry cpu time accounting in C\\n\\nThere is no need for this to be in asm, use the new intrrupt entry wrapper.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"8e708979eb786ac7acc1df2aa1a96fba85185c6c","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/8e708979eb786ac7acc1df2aa1a96fba85185c6c"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc: move NMI entry\\/exit code into wrapper\\n\\nThis moves the common NMI entry and exit code into the interrupt handler\\nwrappers.\\n\\nThis changes the behaviour of soft-NMI (watchdog) and HMI interrupts, and\\nalso MCE interrupts on 64e, by adding missing parts of the NMI entry to\\nthem.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"36e6d6e5954c1c70c282d7616558fa784cac6941","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/36e6d6e5954c1c70c282d7616558fa784cac6941"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s: move NMI soft-mask handling to C\\n\\nSaving and restoring soft-mask state can now be done in C using the\\ninterrupt handler wrapper functions.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"cc2a9bd01aa355fcc841cac192561801e786c298","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/cc2a9bd01aa355fcc841cac192561801e786c298"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"powerpc\\/64s: runlatch interrupt handling in C\\n\\nThere is no need for this to be in asm, use the new intrrupt entry wrapper.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"8d2468e9385ae3010462e0753369f771315e45b3","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux\\/commits\\/8d2468e9385ae3010462e0753369f771315e45b3"}],"distinct_size":"21","head":"47dcbe6d9a63af3312c212a6bba681535ab5381c","push_id":"6285849703","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/_v4_21_21__powerpc_64s__power4_nap_fixup_in_C_mbox_powerpc\\/merge","size":"21"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"50888396","name":"ruscur\\/linux","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/linux"},"type":"PushEvent"}
