{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/482276?","display_login":"Benjamin-Dobell","gravatar_id":"","id":"482276","login":"Benjamin-Dobell","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/Benjamin-Dobell"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:58Z","id":"14690752327","payload":{"action":"opened","issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"OWNER","body":"Presently only named fields are suggested\\/completed.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor example:\\r\\n\\r\\n```lua\\r\\n---@class Vector\\r\\n---@field x number\\r\\n---@field y number\\r\\n---@field [1] number\\r\\n---@field [2] number\\r\\n\\r\\n---@type Vector\\r\\nlocal myVector\\r\\n\\r\\nmyVector.--<cursor here>\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis will display a completion prompt that only includes the members `x` and `y`. However, it could also suggest `[1]` and `[2]` and upon completion delete the period.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdditionally, index expressions using brackets could similar be completed e.g.\\r\\n\\r\\n```lua\\r\\nmyVector[--<cursor here>\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nIf we\'re going to be completing _all_ fields in brackets then we\'ll presumably want to prioritise primitive indexed fields over regular named fields and vice versa when completing fields after a period.\\r\\n\\r\\nSee https:\\/\\/github.com\\/Benjamin-Dobell\\/IntelliJ-Luanalysis\\/issues\\/27 for initial report.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Considerations \\/ Additional Thoughts\\r\\n\\r\\nWe\'re only going to be completing primitives, but what about aliases? e.g.\\r\\n\\r\\n```lua\\r\\n---@alias Color \\"Red\\" | \\"Blue\\"\\r\\n\\r\\n---@class Wall\\r\\n---@field color Color\\r\\n\\r\\n---@type Wall\\r\\nlocal wall\\r\\n\\r\\nwall.--<cursor here>\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nShould we suggest \\"Red\\" and \\"Blue\\"?\\r\\n\\r\\nWe certainly can, however completion prompts ought to be _very_ responsive, so minimising work is a good idea 😕 ","comments":"0","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/Benjamin-Dobell\\/IntelliJ-Luanalysis\\/issues\\/28\\/comments","creat