_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bfjelds\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bfjelds\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bfjelds\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/bfjelds"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\\r\\n\\r\\n`kubectl` validates (some?) specs when these are applied.\\r\\n\\r\\n`Configurations` (Akri CRD) are not validated and this permits user-error and other mistakes to escape.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Is your feature request related to a way you would like Akri extended? Please describe.**\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring development of Zeroconf, I inadvertently broker the YAML spec for the Broker:\\r\\n\\r\\n```YAML\\r\\napiVersion: akri.sh\\/v0\\r\\nkind: Configuration\\r\\nmetadata:\\r\\n  name: zeroconf\\r\\nspec:\\r\\n  protocol:\\r\\n    zeroconf:\\r\\n      kind: \\"_rust._tcp\\"\\r\\n      port: 8888\\r\\n      txtRecords:\\r\\n        project: akri\\r\\n        protocol: zeroconf\\r\\n        component: avahi-publish\\r\\n  capacity: 1\\r\\n  brokerPodSpec:\\r\\n    imagePullSecrets: # Container Registry secret\\r\\n      - name: ghcr\\r\\n    containers:\\r\\n      - name: zeroconf-broker\\r\\n        image: ghcr.io\\/dazwilkin\\/zeroconf-broker@sha256:993e5b8d....\\r\\n    resources: <----------------------------- INCORRECTLY INDENTED AFTER EDIT\\r\\n              limits: \\r\\n                \\"{{PLACEHOLDER}}\\": \\"1\\"\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThe result was that, while Brokers were deployed, environment variables were not mounted correctly in the Pod.\\r\\n\\r\\nIt was only after lengthy debugging that we uncovered the error:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bash\\r\\nkubectl get pod\\/akri-zeroconf-9e1938-pod --output=yaml\\r\\n\\r\\nspec:\\r\\n  containers:\\r\\n  - image: ghcr.io\\/dazwilkin\\/zeroconf-broker@sha256:993e5b8d...\\r\\n    imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent\\r\\n    name: zeroconf-broker\\r\\n    resources: {}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nThis may (!?) have been mitigated were the Configuration validated upon apply.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe the solution you\'d like**\\r\\n\\r\\n`kubectl apply --filename=.\\/some-akri-config.yaml`\\r\\n\\r\\nWould yield e.g.:\\r\\n\\r\\n```console\\r\\nerror: error parsing .\\/some-akri-config.yaml: line XX: something wrong described\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\n**Describe alternatives you\'ve considered**\\r\\n\\r\\nBeing less stupid ;-)\\r\\n\\r\\nThis is the convention with Kubernetes and would be a useful addition.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Additional context**\\r\\n\\r\\nSee: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/177\\r\\n","comments":"25","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/180\\/comments","created_at":"2020-12-17T21:55:58Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/180\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/180","id":"770400530","labels":[{"color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","id":"2413407567","name":"enhancement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDEzNDA3NTY3","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/labels\\/enhancement"}],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/180\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU3NzA0MDA1MzA=","number":"180","repository_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri","state":"open","title":"Consider implementing a validator for Configurations","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:38:58Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/deislabs\\/akri\\/issues\\/180","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars3.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/1022400?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/DazWilkin\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/DazWilkin\\/followers","following_url":"