{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/1144029?","display_login":"summii","gravatar_id":"","id":"1144029","login":"summii","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/summii"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:02Z","id":"14690752598","payload":{"before":"c244d7d0dab137dc3bdbeaf1bacf8b936044344c","commits":[{"author":{"email":"3e66f25a5e2271dd1ee955aa41a5b2a1ba1b1fa6@sumeets-MacBook-Pro.local","name":"sumeet bhadana"},"distinct":true,"message":"Test branch","sha":"6b6dbb2976abb9af18f513a8d87b58ed3ca2ef0b","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/summii\\/newrepo-test\\/commits\\/6b6dbb2976abb9af18f513a8d87b58ed3ca2ef0b"}],"distinct_size":"1","head":"6b6dbb2976abb9af18f513a8d87b58ed3ca2ef0b","push_id":"6285849967","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/branch-test","size":"1"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"326223538","name":"summii\\/newrepo-test","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/summii\\/newrepo-test"},"type":"PushEvent"}
{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/43373?","display_login":"npepinpe","gravatar_id":"","id":"43373","login":"npepinpe","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:02Z","id":"14690752600","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/17767077?","gravatar_id":"","id":"17767077","login":"zeebe-io","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/zeebe-io"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Looking at the long running benchmark from the last 2 days (ignore that zeebe 1 is missing, it never started because the node pool is full - oops!)\\r\\n\\r\\n![Screenshot from 2021-01-02 17-17-44](https:\\/\\/user-images.githubusercontent.com\\/43373\\/103461391-760f3d80-4d1e-11eb-9c66-f9c04344cced.png)\\r\\n\\r\\nAs you can see, memory is fairly stable - note that here Zeebe 2 is leader for 2 partitions (and has been since the beginning! surprisingly no role changes occurred), and Zeebe 0 leader for 1.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you check the smap output on Zeebe 2, you get:\\r\\n\\r\\n```\\r\\nRss:            13000348 kB\\r\\nPss:            12067853 kB\\r\\nPss_Anon:         555992 kB\\r\\nPss_File:       11511861 kB\\r\\nPss_Shmem:             0 kB\\r\\nShared_Clean:    1398560 kB\\r\\nShared_Dirty:          0 kB\\r\\nPrivate_Clean:  11045780 kB\\r\\nPrivate_Dirty:    556008 kB\\r\\nReferenced:     13000348 kB\\r\\nAnonymous:        555992 kB\\r\\nLazyFree:              0 kB\\r\\nAnonHugePages:         0 kB\\r\\nShmemPmdMapped:        0 kB\\r\\nShared_Hugetlb:        0 kB\\r\\nPrivate_Hugetlb:       0 kB\\r\\nSwap:                  0 kB\\r\\nSwapPss:               0 kB\\r\\nLocked:                0 kB\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom this, you can see almost all of our memory is from mapped files (i.e. `Pss_File`), so it\'s mostly the OS page cache, and what we actually allocated via malloc and such is 555992 kB (about ~500 mB). The OOM killer deals very well with this as it will always force the page cache to drop pages first before killing a process, and looking at the WSS graph above we see this happening regularly.\\r\\n\\r\\nHowever, what this means for us is when we want to explain how much memory to provision, we need to talk about additional things:\\r\\n\\r\\n- memory to provision per partition for the broker\'s long living allocations (e.g. dispatcher)\\r\\n- JVM heap memory\\r\\n- RocksDB block cache and memtable allocations\\r\\n- some % of memory for the OS page cache to allow both RocksDB and our log readers to work efficiently\\r\\n\\r\\nThat last one is something we need to figure out - how much memory should be provisioned that we won\'t use directly but will be available for buffered I\\/O?\\r\\n\\r\\nSo for example, in this load test, we budgeted 512Mb for RocksDB per partition for cache, memtable, index, filter, etc. - everything but temporary overhead during flushing and compaction (see for example the Memtable wiki page, which shows that `SkipList` memtable requires constant extra memory for flushing). That means for Zeebe 2, we have about 1GB for sure, and let\'s say some constant overhead, let\'s say 25%, ~256Mb - honestly I have no idea, but let\'s worst case this. Then we have so 25% of the requested memory for JVM heap (so 3GB - though we are using only 1GB so far), and at peak we have something like 17 segments (seems we export too slow now), which all have a writer which maps our segment files entirely (512MB), which theoretically have been read such that their pages will be loaded in the page cache and only evicted under memory pressure. We can see the WSS regularly goes up to 11GB (out of 12GB requested), but gets dropped back down rather hard, which would corroborate the hypothesis that most of the memory is page cache - which is also corroborated by the smap output itself (since only about ~500MB are anonymous allocations, the rest are all mapped from files).\\r\\n\\r\\nInteresting would be to run a load test with less memory available - here we see a leader of 2 partitions with a stable RSS of 4GB. So let\'s say 2GB per partition, we can try running with 6GB and see how stable it remains under constant load for a long period of time.","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:02Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002#issuecomment-753495629","id":"753495629","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTYyOQ==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:02Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495629","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars0.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/43373?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/npepinpe","id":"43373","login":"npepinpe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMzcz","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/npepinpe"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"**Description**\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrently we use multiple column families ~ 50. This comes with a price, since each column family has his own mem table, index and bloom filter.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe can see [here](https:\\/\\/github.com\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/3988) how problematic this is.\\r\\n\\r\\nActually I\'m not really sure whether we need the different column families at all.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n> The main idea behind Column Families is that they share the write-ahead log and don\'t share memtables and table files. By sharing write-ahead logs we get awesome benefit of atomic writes. By separating memtables and table files, we are able to configure column families independently and delete them quickly.\\r\\n> _from:_ https:\\/\\/github.com\\/facebook\\/rocksdb\\/wiki\\/Column-Families\\r\\n\\r\\nSince we not really want to dynamically delete nor create new ones. Furthermore we don\'t want to configure them separately since usage of the different column families is totally use case dependent. That is why I see no big value in them.\\r\\n\\r\\nI think it is still possible to use our abstraction and the related enum. If we would use only one column family we would use the Enum.value as key marker and put it as first byte in the keys. In that way the keys are still ordered and we can easily seek and access them. This would mean that we only need to change the implementation for now. We would probably gain a better memory consumption. Still we need to check how the performance would be affected by that.","comments":"16","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002\\/comments","created_at":"2020-03-06T15:13:17Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002","id":"576994091","labels":[{"color":"88ccff","default":false,"description":"Issue might impact the memory consumption.","id":"2455130256","name":"Impact: Memory Consumption","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDU1MTMwMjU2","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Impact:%20Memory%20Consumption"},{"color":"88ccff","default":false,"description":"","id":"1965843664","name":"Impact: Performance","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTY1ODQzNjY0","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Impact:%20Performance"},{"color":"FFFF00","default":false,"description":"","id":"2018095177","name":"Priority: Mid","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDE4MDk1MTc3","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Priority:%20Mid"},{"color":"5e76e5","default":false,"description":"All issues which are part of a research or investigation regarding any topic.","id":"2455128826","name":"Research","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNDU1MTI4ODI2","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Research"},{"color":"ffddbb","default":false,"description":"","id":"1150260843","name":"Scope: broker","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwMjYwODQz","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Scope:%20broker"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"description":"","id":"1150248446","name":"Status: Planned","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwMjQ4NDQ2","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Status:%20Planned"},{"color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"","id":"1150254280","name":"Type: Maintenance","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTUwMjU0Mjgw","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/labels\\/Type:%20Maintenance"}],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NzY5OTQwOTE=","number":"4002","repository_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe","state":"open","title":"Can we drop multiple ColumnFamily support","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:02Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/zeebe-io\\/zeebe\\/issues\\/4002","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars2.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/2758593?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/Zelldon\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/Zelldon\\/followers","following_url":"