{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/7971489?","display_login":"jollaman999","gravatar_id":"","id":"7971489","login":"jollaman999","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jollaman999"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:04Z","id":"14690752759","payload":{"before":"25cfd660535d5879d7eea2d53d5ede2c9d8d4527","commits":[{"author":{"email":"de992550493871feb39ca8e386f97a693c2c93e9@archlinux.us","name":"John Audia"},"distinct":true,"message":"kernel: bump 5.4 to 5.4.82\\n\\nRemoved since included upstream and could be reverse-applied by quilt:\\n  backport-5.4\\/315-v5.10-usbnet-ipeth-fix-connectivity-with-ios-14.patch\\n\\nRemaining modifications made by update_kernel.sh\\n\\nBuild system: x86_64\\nBuild-tested: ipq806x\\/R7800, ath79\\/generic, bcm27xx\\/bcm2711\\nRun-tested: ipq806x\\/R7800\\n\\nNo dmesg regressions, everything functional\\n\\nSigned-off-by: John Audia <graysky@archlinux.us>\\nTested-by: Curtis Deptuck <curtdept@me.com> [build\\/run x86_64]","sha":"3a91c34088c0734c009d272e839fa201a1129a85","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/3a91c34088c0734c009d272e839fa201a1129a85"},{"author":{"email":"ac73eed4b8a8c9127255a2696c52b2e7503720b8@gmail.com","name":"Brian Norris"},"distinct":true,"message":"scripts\\/feeds: warn when skipping core package override\\n\\nOtherwise, a n00b like myself can get quite confused when moving a\\npackage from core to feeds, for example.\\n\\n(Hint: one *really* needs to clear out the tmp\\/info\\/.packageinfo...\\nentries for the stale package, but \'-f\' works as well.)\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Brian Norris <computersforpeace@gmail.com>","sha":"1b4a44969732481f3a932e149cbbffa1290ad2cd","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/1b4a44969732481f3a932e149cbbffa1290ad2cd"},{"author":{"email":"42a785db5cac8022043ae11d140a69ce324665dc@gmail.com","name":"Hans Dedecker"},"distinct":true,"message":"odhcp6c: update to latest git HEAD\\n\\n0ffa3a3 dhcpv6: harden reconfigure logic\\n3999b6d dhcpv6: rework DHCPv6 message to string implementation\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Hans Dedecker <dedeckeh@gmail.com>","sha":"c4968c9d381be76f1704a8d36d9a6b8b8d9e70ac","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/c4968c9d381be76f1704a8d36d9a6b8b8d9e70ac"},{"author":{"email":"1d6e1cf70ec6f9ab28d3ea4b27a49a77654d370e@aparcar.org","name":"Paul Spooren"},"distinct":true,"message":"iftop: remove package\\n\\nThe package has no reason to be in openwrt.git. Move it to packages.git.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>\\nAcked-by: Jo-Philipp Wich <jo@mein.io>","sha":"a59c47e496d468e7bacec36595c8473ffffe47b1","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/a59c47e496d468e7bacec36595c8473ffffe47b1"},{"author":{"email":"1d6e1cf70ec6f9ab28d3ea4b27a49a77654d370e@aparcar.org","name":"Paul Spooren"},"distinct":true,"message":"opkg: remove legacy dist and extra_data\\n\\nefb26a3 libopkg: remove \\"extra_data\\" option\\n1d67ab7 libopkg: remove support for \\"dist\\" config\\n\\nReduces opkg size by about 400 Bytes.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>","sha":"dadd8174a8ef98d7a8fbd23a7b98808c3060548b","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/dadd8174a8ef98d7a8fbd23a7b98808c3060548b"},{"author":{"email":"31c0c8d0bc39ae8caff8ead56348d756336c2a13@nic.cz","name":"Karel Kočí"},"distinct":true,"message":"scripts\\/feeds: fix preference of package install\\n\\nThe previous behavior prefered same feed for dependent packages as\\ninitial package. This caused inconsitency in installation of packages.\\nThe difference was if two feeds provide same package (different version)\\nthere was different result if you executed install for that specific\\nversion compared to install for package depending on it from different\\nfeed.\\n\\nThis ensures that preferred feed is propagated without change and\\nselected feed is used only really for package it was selected for.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Karel Kočí <karel.koci@nic.cz>","sha":"8a0801369b0aa087c583b5e67101ebdeaf575fda","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/8a0801369b0aa087c583b5e67101ebdeaf575fda"},{"author":{"email":"3d0f3b9ddcacec30c4008c5e030e6c13a478cb4f@makrotopia.org","name":"Daniel Golle"},"distinct":true,"message":"config: add big EXPERIMENTAL option\\n\\nAs discussed in the today\'s (2020-12-10) meeting, add a new option to\\nmenuconfig to group the selection of all experimental features to be\\nselected by default.\\nDevelopers are recommended to make use of this new symbol to guard\\nnew features.\\nOther developers and community members should feel encouraged to\\nbuild with this flag enabled to help testing and provide feedback.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>","sha":"79795e41fed1f04da674e5b2d82c304ffd6250dc","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/79795e41fed1f04da674e5b2d82c304ffd6250dc"},{"author":{"email":"da711e431b4308466c0a85448993d2d5190625f5@gmail.com","name":"Daniel González Cabanelas"},"distinct":true,"message":"bcm63xx: DGND3700v1: use the real board name\\n\\nThe Netgear DGND3700v1\\/DGND3800B shows kernel redundant info at the board\\nmessage, already provided by the machine info message.\\n\\nUse the real board name which is silkscreened on the PCB and used in the\\nstock firmware header.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Daniel González Cabanelas <dgcbueu@gmail.com>","sha":"722b5fcdb754a2f85828c0527ec1bbb6bcdf155f","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/722b5fcdb754a2f85828c0527ec1bbb6bcdf155f"},{"author":{"email":"c34ce55a28cd60b1fd1e5d364f45dadd369652f2@gmail.com","name":"Eneas U de Queiroz"},"distinct":true,"message":"wolfssl: add lighty support, skip crypttests\\n\\nTnis adds the --enable-lighty option to configure, enabling the minimum\\nAPI needed to run lighttpd, in the packages feed.  Size increase is\\nabout 120 bytes for arm_cortex-a9_vfpv3-d16.\\n\\nWhile at it, speed up build by disabling crypt bench\\/test.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Eneas U de Queiroz <cotequeiroz@gmail.com>","sha":"8536e175fb8bd4cd40ea75beb9606b31ac5888ce","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/8536e175fb8bd4cd40ea75beb9606b31ac5888ce"},{"author":{"email":"c34ce55a28cd60b1fd1e5d364f45dadd369652f2@gmail.com","name":"Eneas U de Queiroz"},"distinct":true,"message":"wolfssl: compile with --enable-opensslall\\n\\nThis enables all OpenSSL API available.  It is required to avoid some\\nsilent failures, such as when performing client certificate validation.\\n\\nPackage size increases from 356.6K to 374.7K for\\narm_cortex-a9_vfpv3-d16.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Eneas U de Queiroz <cotequeiroz@gmail.com>","sha":"a53f5ba44d2aafc3c553a136a805960bfba87bd9","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/a53f5ba44d2aafc3c553a136a805960bfba87bd9"},{"author":{"email":"f0d4d86d9c7002e67e6ae7bb5596bc0afa7b4c3a@true.cz","name":"Petr Štetiar"},"distinct":true,"message":"wolfssl: fix broken wolfSSL_X509_check_host\\n\\nBackport upstream post 4.5.0 fix for broken wolfSSL_X509_check_host().\\n\\nReferences: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/wolfSSL\\/wolfssl\\/issues\\/3329\\nSigned-off-by: Petr Štetiar <ynezz@true.cz>","sha":"0addbdbbd5fd7221972bc3a382b57bdab9399017","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/0addbdbbd5fd7221972bc3a382b57bdab9399017"},{"author":{"email":"46f1a0bd5592a2f9244ca321b129902a06b53e03@johnthomson.fastmail.com.au","name":"John Thomson"},"distinct":true,"message":"package\\/base-files: caldata: use dd iflag fullblock\\n\\nThis dd flag ensures that the requested size\\nis retrieved from pipes or special filesystems (if available).\\n\\nWithout this flag, on multi-core systems,\\nPiped or special filesystem data can be truncated\\nwhen a size greater than PIPE_BUF is requested.\\n\\nFixes: FS#3494\\nFixes: 7557e7f (\\"package\\/base-files: caldata: work around dd\'s\\nlimitation\\")\\nCc: Thibaut VARÈNE <hacks@slashdirt.org>\\n\\nSigned-off-by: John Thomson <git@johnthomson.fastmail.com.au>","sha":"94139042490a9ca076aaa37105efce56e1e1d012","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/94139042490a9ca076aaa37105efce56e1e1d012"},{"author":{"email":"5be01acc1933caa4a9c30981945cd508cfd9d280@protonmail.com","name":"Rafał Mikrut"},"distinct":true,"message":"realtek: Fix self assignment\\n\\nCppcheck shows self initialization error, which is an obvious bug.\\n\\nBasing on logic of similar fragment below I assigned to this variable,\\nvalue `RTL838X_LED_GLB_CTRL` which I think is proper.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Rafał Mikrut <mikrutrafal@protonmail.com>","sha":"b5ee67706955b6de563b209300cacaf0cb2e6fe2","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/b5ee67706955b6de563b209300cacaf0cb2e6fe2"},{"author":{"email":"5be01acc1933caa4a9c30981945cd508cfd9d280@protonmail.com","name":"Rafał Mikrut"},"distinct":true,"message":"realtek: Add missing case in switch statement\\n\\nCppcheck shows here duplicated break.\\n\\nCode `state->speed = SPEED_1000;` will be never executed because above\\nit there is break statement.\\n\\nAlmost identical statement is placed in another realtek driver\\nhttps:\\/\\/github.com\\/openwrt\\/openwrt\\/blob\\/18a53d43d646290053eff4736ec852efcf6bf510\\/target\\/linux\\/realtek\\/files-5.4\\/drivers\\/net\\/dsa\\/rtl83xx\\/dsa.c#L286-L294\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Rafał Mikrut <mikrutrafal@protonmail.com>","sha":"1ba759cd3043b8e789f74de71793312dcbc28c0d","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/1ba759cd3043b8e789f74de71793312dcbc28c0d"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: enable back DROPBEAR_USE_PASSWORD_ENV\\n\\nthis option was disabled in 2011 and these long nine years showed us that change was definitely wrong.\\n\\nbinary size cost is much less than 1k.\\n\\ntested on ath79\\/generic:\\n  bin: 215128 -> 215128 (no change)\\n  ipk: 111108 -> 111183 (+75b)\\n\\nFixes: 3c801b3dc0359 (\\"tune some more options by default to decrease size\\")\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>","sha":"b84ac0ffae5b3d2fd342228d5c4fb042707cad45","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/b84ac0ffae5b3d2fd342228d5c4fb042707cad45"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: reorder options in Configure recipe\\n\\nput static options at first place, then place configurable options.\\nalso put DROPBEAR_ECC right before DROPBEAR_ECC_FULL to ease maintainance.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>","sha":"0938abd8cdd35fac8919182a8a6981a6dc4d1b62","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/0938abd8cdd35fac8919182a8a6981a6dc4d1b62"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: rework recipes that configure build\\n\\n- add two helper functions to avoid mistakes with\\n  choice of correct header file to work with\\n- update rules accordingly\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>","sha":"9ecc5d773736c98d35bc12998778f4c2f5e82ccb","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/9ecc5d773736c98d35bc12998778f4c2f5e82ccb"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: roll up recipes into mapping lists\\n\\nthis commit removes manual recipes for options and introduces mapping lists:\\n- DB_OPT_COMMON holds option mappings which are common for all builds;\\n- DB_OPT_CONFIG holds option mappings which are depend on config settings.\\n\\nDB_OPT_COMMON is space-separated list of \'words\', each of them is in format:\\n  \'header_option|value\'\\n\\n\'header_option\' is added with value \'value\' to \'localoptions.h\'.\\n\\nif \'header_option\' is preceded by two exclamation marks (\'!!\')\\nthen option is not added to \'localoptions.h\' but replaced in \'sysoptions.h\'.\\n\\nin short:\\n   option|value - add option to localoptions.h\\n !!option|value - replace option in sysoptions.h\\n\\nDB_OPT_CONFIG is space-separated list of \'words\', each of them is in format:\\n  \'header_option|config_variable|value_enabled|value_disabled\'\\n\\n\'header_option\' is handled likewise in DB_OPT_COMMON.\\n\\nif \'config_variable\' is enabled (technically: not disabled)\\nthen \'header_option\' is set to \'value_enabled\' and \'value_disabled\' otherwise.\\n\\nin short:\\n   option|config|enabled|disabled = add option to localoptions.h\\n !!option|config|enabled|disabled = replace option in sysoptions.h\\n\\n   option := (config) ? enabled : disabled\\n\\nIf you\'re not sure that option\'s value doesn\'t have \'|\' within - add your recipe\\nmanually right after \'$(Build\\/Configure\\/dropbear_headers)\' and write some words\\nabout your decision.\\n\\nPS about two exclamation marks:\\nearly idea was to use one exclamation mark to denote such header options\\nbut then i thought single exclamation mark may be overlooked by mistake.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>","sha":"e8869775ea29a62bfc314d772dcd120f4579fcec","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/e8869775ea29a62bfc314d772dcd120f4579fcec"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: add ssh-askpass support in configuration\\n\\nbinary size cost is much less than 1k.\\n\\ntested on ath79\\/generic:\\n  bin: 215128 -> 215132 (+4b)\\n  ipk: 111183 -> 111494 (+311b)\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>","sha":"d0d0d6d1a3df5bd3090f4cb7951dc5a0228e8775","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/d0d0d6d1a3df5bd3090f4cb7951dc5a0228e8775"},{"author":{"email":"678b1f838d653932c3f1b8054223272fc928673a@gmail.com","name":"Konstantin Demin"},"distinct":true,"message":"dropbear: bump package version\\n\\nBump package version after previous changes.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Konstantin Demin <rockdrilla@gmail.com>\\n[added missing commit description]\\nSigned-off-by: Petr Štetiar <ynezz@true.cz>","sha":"803b8ddbd385ac347e18bc70054ddff3a0dc3435","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt\\/commits\\/803b8ddbd385ac347e18bc70054ddff3a0dc3435"}],"distinct_size":"229","head":"2db1c84ffd16ea59f043d8b7d1051134133e5e0c","push_id":"6285850049","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/master","size":"229"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"89925905","name":"jollaman999\\/openwrt","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/jollaman999\\/openwrt"},"type":"PushEvent"}
