3b0abb6b854eccd8f3a87ac728","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/36329827386d163b0abb6b854eccd8f3a87ac728"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: move cpu_wake out of job_lock, only wake if necessary\\n\\nThere is no need to keep the IPI initiation under the job_lock.\\nIf the target does wake after the job is queued and before we can\\nsend the IPI, it will check for new jobs.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"84e824ea5c86314214fe4c707a094e88d14fbd28","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/84e824ea5c86314214fe4c707a094e88d14fbd28"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: make cpu idle states simpler\\n\\nin_idle is true for any kind of idle. This is not used anywhere\\nexcept for state assertions, but it could be used to remove the\\nidle_lock and global counter if that becomes a significant\\ncost.\\n\\nin_sleep is true for sleep that requires an IPI to wake up.\\n\\nin_job_sleep is true for sleep that wants an IPI sent after a job is\\nqueued, and implies in_sleep.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"d5259358b69c326a1a349bddacaa3181ff849d28","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/d5259358b69c326a1a349bddacaa3181ff849d28"}],"distinct_size":"5","head":"d5259358b69c326a1a349bddacaa3181ff849d28","push_id":"6285850402","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/_5_6__core_cpu__make_cpu_idle_states_simpler_mbox_master","size":"5"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"52412231","name":"ruscur\\/skiboot","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot"},"type":"PushEvent"}
