{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/17824796?","display_login":"varnastadeus","gravatar_id":"","id":"17824796","login":"varnastadeus","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/varnastadeus"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:14Z","id":"14690753393","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/31009335?","gravatar_id":"","id":"31009335","login":"ng-select","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/ng-select"},"payload":{"action":"reopened","issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"**Describe the bug**\\r\\n\\r\\nIf I define `groupBy=\\"group\\"` but none of the items have a `group` property, `ng-select` will behave oddly when searching for items and selecting searched items (e.g. multiple items will appear selected; cannot select searched item).\\r\\n\\r\\nThis also affects `ng-select`s with the `multiple` option set.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Reproducbile example**\\r\\n\\r\\nSimply add `groupBy=\\"group\\"` to the `ng-select` of this example: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/tree\\/master\\/src\\/demo\\/app\\/examples\\/search-default-example (use the StackBlitz of the first example here: https:\\/\\/ng-select.github.io\\/ng-select#\\/search)\\r\\n\\r\\n**To Reproduce** \\r\\n\\r\\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Create an `ng-select` with `groupBy=\\"group\\"` and `items=\\"items\\"` where no item in `items` has a `group` property.\\r\\n1. Use the search function of the `ng-select` (type something into it)\\r\\n1. Select random item\\r\\n1. Use the search function again\\r\\n1. Select a different random item\\r\\n1. Use the search function again\\r\\n1. Both previously selected items will have a \\"selected\\" style\\r\\n\\r\\n**Expected behavior**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhen none of the items have the group property defined in `groupBy`, `ng-select` should behave as if there were no groups and no `groupBy`.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Screenshots**\\r\\n\\r\\n![image](https:\\/\\/user-images.githubusercontent.com\\/8314616\\/82730875-f5558100-9cfa-11ea-88e3-263233e2adc8.png)\\r\\n\\r\\n**Versions**\\r\\n\\r\\nUsing latest `ng-select` 4.0.0 version. Tested in Windows and Linux, Chrome and Firefox.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Workaround**\\r\\n\\r\\nFor now I\'m doing something like the following in the HTML:\\r\\n```html\\r\\n<ng-select [items]=\\"items\\" [groupBy]=\\"groupBy\\"><\\/ng-select>\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAnd the following in the TS:\\r\\n```ts\\r\\nget groupBy(): \'group\' | null {\\r\\n  return this.items.some(item => \'group\' in item) ? \'group\' : null;\\r\\n}\\r\\n```","comments":"3","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/issues\\/1628\\/comments","created_at":"2020-05-23T12:51:46Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/issues\\/1628\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/issues\\/1628","id":"623654344","labels":[{"color":"618abf","default":false,"description":"","id":"1623327177","name":"stale","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNjIzMzI3MTc3","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/labels\\/stale"}],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/issues\\/1628\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2MjM2NTQzNDQ=","number":"1628","repository_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select","state":"open","title":"Odd search behaviour with `groupBy` when no items have a group","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:14Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ng-select\\/ng-select\\/issues\\/1628","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars3.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/8314616?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/nunocastromartins\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/nunocastromartins\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/nunocastromartins\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.gi