{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/5637090?","display_login":"ruscur","gravatar_id":"","id":"5637090","login":"ruscur","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ruscur"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:39:40Z","id":"14690754897","payload":{"before":"d5259358b69c326a1a349bddacaa3181ff849d28","commits":[{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: rewrite idle synchronisation\\n\\nThis changes CPU idle synchronisation to always kick all other CPUs\\nout of idle code first whenever idle settings (pm_enabled, IPIs, sreset\\netc) are to be changed.\\n\\nCurrently this is somewhat racy and not obviously correct, with\\npm_enabled changing while in low level idle routines, which does\\nresult in messages like \\"cpu_idle_p9 called pm disabled\\".\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"e728be664362cb093e812f0237acf98173eee61c","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/e728be664362cb093e812f0237acf98173eee61c"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: remove POWER8 IPI loop\\n\\nPOWER8 should not have to loop sending IPIs until the destination\\nwakes up. One should be enough.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"a3cc269041518147aa6b0756ce796748e0d1d483","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/a3cc269041518147aa6b0756ce796748e0d1d483"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: refactor IPI sending\\n\\nPull the IPI sending code into its own function where it is used in\\ntwo places.\\n\\ncpu_wake() already checks in_idle, so its caller does not need to\\ncheck pm_enabled.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"849d87fde747725268c4ad118c33a30615ff3b64","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/849d87fde747725268c4ad118c33a30615ff3b64"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: move cpu_wake out of job_lock, only wake if necessary\\n\\nThere is no need to keep the IPI initiation under the job_lock.\\nIf the target does wake after the job is queued and before we can\\nsend the IPI, it will check for new jobs.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"364821c918406906335c786f535a60bf7bbeb7c0","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/364821c918406906335c786f535a60bf7bbeb7c0"},{"author":{"email":"24829078df5003d9dd1dd871ca2aeb0b1cf95ef4@gmail.com","name":"Nicholas Piggin"},"distinct":true,"message":"core\\/cpu: make cpu idle states simpler\\n\\nin_idle is true for any kind of idle. This is not used anywhere\\nexcept for state assertions, but it could be used to remove the\\nidle_lock and global counter if that becomes a significant\\ncost.\\n\\nin_sleep is true for sleep that requires an IPI to wake up.\\n\\nin_job_sleep is true for sleep that wants an IPI sent after a job is\\nqueued, and implies in_sleep.\\n\\nSigned-off-by: Nicholas Piggin <npiggin@gmail.com>","sha":"c8c5664cadc4a15839bb5db53f63b80d68db8a3c","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot\\/commits\\/c8c5664cadc4a15839bb5db53f63b80d68db8a3c"}],"distinct_size":"5","head":"c8c5664cadc4a15839bb5db53f63b80d68db8a3c","push_id":"6285851456","ref":"refs\\/heads\\/_5_6__core_cpu__make_cpu_idle_states_simpler_mbox_master","size":"5"},"public":true,"repo":{"id":"52412231","name":"ruscur\\/skiboot","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/ruscur\\/skiboot"},"type":"PushEvent"}
