 <tmammare@redhat.com>","sha":"5bff5ed6a1a1117eb0b5f497c681c3d927008143","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/bragaigor\\/openj9\\/commits\\/5bff5ed6a1a1117eb0b5f497c681c3d927008143"},{"author":{"email":"8abd1ff3f747df23e2285ffa6b8768f665774ab2@ca.ibm.com","name":"Babneet Singh"},"distinct":true,"message":"Update linkToInterface for OpenJDK MethodHandles\\n\\nNow, it properly handles:\\n- Private interface methods\\n- j.l.Object methods\\n- vTable offset for the method\\n- iTable index for the method\\n\\nAlso, the latest version of the class is retrieved for the iTable\\nsearch.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Jack Lu <Jack.S.Lu@ibm.com>\\nSigned-off-by: Babneet Singh <sbabneet@ca.ibm.com>","sha":"41fdedde11f2093595ee03a3a716c89050b12cbe","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/bragaigor\\/openj9\\/commits\\/41fdedde11f2093595ee03a3a716c89050b12cbe"},{"author":{"email":"f01769b45afa3192d1151f0936e868bcf12df4fa@ca.ibm.com","name":"Tobi"},"distinct":true,"message":"Merge pull request #11518 from hangshao0\\/JEP390\\n\\nFix exception message on illegal sync on value type\\/value based obj","sha":"83b76ae06e2cf53b8b7017a43c59372ec00b32ef","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/bragaigor\\/openj9\\/commits\\/83b76ae06e2cf53b8b7017a43c59372ec00b32ef"},{"author":{"email":"73675debcd8a436be48ec22211dcf44fe0df0a64@benthomas.ca","name":"Ben Thomas"},"distinct":true,"message":"Simplify ArrayStoreCHK evaluator\\n\\nPreviously, the evaluator for ArrayStoreCHK included duplicate code for\\nperforming write barriers. While this did provide one small optimization\\nbenefit (it avoided performing two null checks for a certain kind of\\nwrite barrier), it required that a lot of very complex code for\\nperforming write barriers be duplicated and would make changes to this\\ncode needlessly difficult due to the way that support is currently\\nwritten.\\n\\nWhile it should be possible to reintroduce this optimization in the\\nfuture, in the interests of simplicity while the write 