ver: I added multiple integration tests (Spring) related to the features (with a high test coverage)\\r\\n- [x]  Server: I implemented the changes with a good performance and prevented too many database calls\\r\\n- [x]  Server: I documented the Java code using JavaDoc style.\\r\\n- [x]  Client: I followed the coding and design guidelines.\\r\\n- [x]  Client: I added multiple integration tests (Jest) related to the features (with a high test coverage)\\r\\n- [x]  Client: I documented the TypeScript code using JSDoc style.\\r\\n- [x]  Client: I added multiple screenshots\\/screencasts of my UI changes\\r\\n- [x]  Client: I translated all the newly inserted strings into German and English\\r\\n\\r\\n### Motivation and Context\\r\\n<!-- Why is this change required? What problem does it solve? -->\\r\\n<!-- If it fixes an open issue, please link to the issue here. -->\\r\\nCurrently zero point exercises are not completely supported on all exercise types for manual assessment and complaints. This PR introduces the support for this.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Description\\r\\n<!-- Describe your changes in detail -->\\r\\n- [x] Extract `getMaxScoreRespectingZeroPointExercises` so that it can be used from other components on server and client\\r\\n- [x] Implement correct use of maxPoints for assessment of Modeling, Text and FileUpload exercises + complaints\\r\\n- [x] Implement correct use of maxPoints for assessment of Programming exercises + complaints\\r\\n\\r\\n### Steps for Testing\\r\\n<!-- Please describe in detail how the reviewer can test your changes. -->\\r\\n\\r\\nNormal exercises:\\r\\n\\r\\n1. Log in to Artemis\\r\\n2. Navigate to Course Administration\\r\\n\\r\\n**Important: test the following 4 cases in 4 different exercises for Programming, Modeling, Text, Quiz and FileUpload:**\\r\\n - [x] 10 points + 0 bonus points\\r\\n - [x] 10 points + 10 bonus points\\r\\n - [x] 0 points + 10 bonus points\\r\\n - [x] 0 points + 0 bonus points\\r\\n\\r\\nTest the following scenario: if a student e.g. has collected 30 points in a course, but the sum of normal points is 20, then the score on the start page of Artemis should show 150%. The score calculation is really critical and has to be absolutely correct!\\r\\nAlso make sure that the instructor page course scores includes the correct calculation based on the sum of normal points and the exported csv file is correct.\\r\\n\\r\\n3. Assess the exercises \\r\\n4. See if everything works as expected\\r\\n5. Complain and assess the complaint\\r\\n6. See if everything works as expected\\r\\n\\r\\n### Test Coverage\\r\\n<!-- Please add the test coverage for all changes files here. You can see this when executing the tests locally (see build.gradle and package.json) or when looking into the corresponding Bamboo build plan -->\\r\\n\\r\\nServer:\\r\\n\\r\\n- Exercise.java: 92%\\r\\n- Result.java: 95%\\r\\n- AssessmentService.java: 88%\\r\\n- ProgrammingAssessmentService.java: 92%\\r\\n- ProgrammingExerciseGradingService.java: 95%\\r\\n\\r\\nClient:\\r\\n\\r\\n- scoreChartPreset.ts: 92%\\r\\n- exercise-utils.ts: 91%\\r\\n- result-detail.component.ts: 95%\\r\\n- code-editor-tutor-assessment-container.component: 81%\\r\\n- text-feedback-conflicts.component.ts: 79%\\r\\n- modeling-assessment.component.ts: 78.95%\\r\\n- score-display.component: 76%\\r\\n- modeling-assessment-editor.component.ts: 72%\\r\\n- text-assessment-base.component.ts: 71%\\r\\n- text-submission-assessment.component: 65%\\r\\n- modeling-submission.component.ts: 55%\\r\\n- file-upload-assessment.component.ts: 33% -> 56% (WIP)\\r\\n\\r\\n### Screenshots\\r\\n<!-- Add screenshots to demonstrate the changes in the UI. -->\\r\\n<!-- Create a GIF file from a screen recording in a docker container https:\\/\\/toub.es\\/2017\\/09\\/11\\/high-quality-gif-with-ffmpeg-and-docker\\/ -->\\r\\n\\r\\nTooltip when bonus points are available:\\r\\n![image](https:\\/\\/user-images.githubusercontent.com\\/33484318\\/103211298-18d35080-4908-11eb-9773-d4