{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/17543446?","display_login":"kubav182","gravatar_id":"","id":"17543446","login":"kubav182","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/kubav182"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:06Z","id":"14690756558","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/7815877?","gravatar_id":"","id":"7815877","login":"spring-cloud","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/spring-cloud"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"NONE","body":"@jonatan-ivanov I could not make not working example, so i tried different use cases with my app and this is what I discovered:\\r\\nThe problem is not variable SPRING_ZIPKIN_ENABLED, but variable SPRING_SLEUTH_MESSAGING_ENABLED=false\\r\\nThis property is now spring.sleuth.messaging.messaging.enabled instead of spring.sleuth.messaging.enabled in previous version. When I change it to SPRING_SLEUTH_MESSAGING_MESSAGING_ENABLED it works fine.\\r\\n\\r\\nBut what is quite strange this error occurs only when I run app in kubernetes, when I run it via docker-compose or as jar it starts fine with that old variable.\\r\\n\\r\\nI would recommend improvement - this class:\\r\\n```\\r\\n@ConfigurationProperties(\\"spring.sleuth.messaging\\")\\r\\npublic class SleuthMessagingProperties\\r\\n```\\r\\nshould not contain inner class `public static class Messaging`\\r\\nand fields inside this static class should be just fields of SleuthMessagingProperties to prevent doubling .messaging","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:06Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/spring-cloud\\/spring-cloud-sleuth\\/issues\\/1813#issuecomment-753495815","id":"753495815","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/spring-cloud\\/spring-cloud-sleuth\\/issues\\/1813","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTgxNQ==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:06Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/spring-cloud\\/spring-cloud-sleuth\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495815","user":{"