{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/13067016?","display_login":"PJ-Finlay","gravatar_id":"","id":"13067016","login":"PJ-Finlay","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:07Z","id":"14690756611","payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"I [asked about length_penalty on the OpenNMT forum](https:\\/\\/forum.opennmt.net\\/t\\/suggested-value-for-length-penalty\\/4134) and it sounds like ideally this would fine-tuned for individual language pairs. For now I\'m just setting it to 0.2 which seems like a better default then 0 based on the linked paper and keeps the simplicity of one pipeline for all languages.\\r\\n\\r\\nI\'m closing this issue now but leaving the other one open for Chinese translations.","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:06Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4#issuecomment-753495819","id":"753495819","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTgxOQ==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:06Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495819","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars0.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/13067016?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/PJ-Finlay","id":"13067016","login":"PJ-Finlay","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDY3MDE2","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/PJ-Finlay"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"While investigating using argos-translate as a library, I have noticed non-deterministic results when translating a short test string \\"Hello world!\\" using your pre-trained models.  For English -> Russian, it returns \\"Здравствуй мир!\\" on some hosts, and \\"Здравствуй!\\" on others.  The results on a given host _are_ deterministic on repeated runs and environments (at least in my testing so far).\\r\\n\\r\\nI first tried to follow the advice here thinking it could be a random seed issue to no avail:\\r\\nhttps:\\/\\/github.com\\/OpenNMT\\/OpenNMT-py\\/issues\\/392\\r\\nhttps:\\/\\/github.com\\/pytorch\\/pytorch\\/issues\\/7068#issuecomment-484918113\\r\\n\\r\\nI was not able to determine any significant differences between hosts (both running on cpu), and the output of ct2_verbose is identical:\\r\\n```\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] CPU: GenuineIntel (SSE4.1=true, AVX=true, AVX2=true)\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] Selected CPU ISA: AVX2\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] Use Intel MKL: true\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] SGEMM CPU backend: MKL\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] GEMM_S16 CPU backend: MKL\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] GEMM_S8 CPU backend: MKL (u8s8 preferred: true)\\r\\n[ct2_verbose] Use packed GEMM: false\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nManually setting `num_hypotheses=2` in the ctranslate2 Translator shows that it appears to be a score difference:\\r\\n```\\r\\nHost #1:\\r\\n\\t{\'tokens\': [\'▁З\', \'д\', \'рав\', \'ству\', \'й\', \'!\'], \'score\': -2.7840166091918945}\\r\\n\\t{\'tokens\': [\'▁З\', \'д\', \'рав\', \'ству\', \'й\', \'▁мир\', \'!\'], \'score\': -2.841048240661621}\\r\\n\\r\\nHost #2:\\r\\n\\t{\'tokens\': [\'▁З\', \'д\', \'рав\', \'ству\', \'й\', \'▁мир\', \'!\'], \'score\': -2.7670412063598633}\\r\\n\\t{\'tokens\': [\'▁З\', \'д\', \'рав\', \'ству\', \'й\', \'!\'], \'score\': -2.7944717407226562}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nSetting ``beam_size=1`` so it uses greedy search _did_ produce the same result on both hosts, but I don\'t think that is a valid solution.\\r\\n\\r\\nI created a gist to provide some debugging output, and didn\'t notice any difference in the actual argos-translate parsing logic, so it seems to be much deeper:  https:\\/\\/gist.github.com\\/mikemoritz\\/a5bf76193ccb16d018a1af9ec584fb41\\r\\n\\r\\nMy questions are:\\r\\n- Are there other options you would recommend setting to increase the likelihood of deterministic results?  If so, could these be surfaced as options within argos-translate?\\r\\n- Is it possible that \\"Hello world!\\" is a bad test string?  If so, do you have any recommendations?\\r\\n- Do you think it could still be a random seed issue that may need to be implemented within argos-translate?\\r\\n- Is there additional debugging within ctranslate2 and\\/or torch that you would recommend to highlight differences between the hosts?\\r\\n\\r\\nThanks!","comments":"5","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4\\/comments","created_at":"2020-12-17T18:47:34Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4","id":"770283690","labels":[{"color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","id":"1969201448","name":"enhancement","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxOTY5MjAxNDQ4","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/labels\\/enhancement"}],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/argosopentech\\/argos-translate\\/issues\\/4\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU3NzAyODM2OTA=","number":"4","repository_url"