{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/44363554?","display_login":"ianinthefuture","gravatar_id":"","id":"44363554","login":"ianinthefuture","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/ianinthefuture"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:23Z","id":"14690757800","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/71455464?","gravatar_id":"","id":"71455464","login":"x-station","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/x-station"},"payload":{"action":"opened","issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"I\'ve just received back my PS1 (PAL 5502) with both a PS1Digital and XStation installed - both do work, have been updated by me to latest firmware, and both have been well installed as far as I can tell, though I\'m no expert.\\r\\n\\r\\nBut I\'ve been seeing FMV intros skipping and glitching - the thing is, **it doesn\'t happen every time** and, **sometimes, is fixed by a soft reset**. But it isn\'t always fixed that way - **it might take one reset, it might take 10**, it\'s completely inconsistent.\\r\\n\\r\\n- I\'ve mainly been testing using Tekken 3, it has three intro vids. Sometimes the main one skipped, the second one didn\'t and the third one did. Sometimes they all did. Sometimes none did. As I say, it\'s inconsistent.\\r\\n\\r\\n**I\'ve made some vids of Tekken 3, here:** https:\\/\\/drive.google.com\\/drive\\/folders\\/1-j5Y-L_8b7UH5fKPrcugdy-lrJLWf-U_?usp=sharing \\r\\n\\r\\n- Trying it with Command and Conquer Red Alert Retaliation either results in both the FMV intro and in-game music skipping, or neither skipping.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Trying it with G-Police is an interesting one, as it has about six separate videos to open the game (three logo vids, three story vids) - sometimes the first and second skip, the third, fourth and fifth don\'t, and the sixth does. Sometimes they all skip. Sometimes the first, second, and sixth don\'t, while the others do. I\'ve no idea of the pattern.\\r\\n\\r\\n- I\'ve tried with five different SD cards, four micro, one full size - Sandisk Extreme 64GB U1 \\/ Sandisk Ultra 64GB U1 \\/ Sandisk Extreme Pro 1TB U3 \\/ Lexar 1667x 128GB U3 V60 (full size SD) \\/ unbranded U3 256GB U3, makes no difference.\\r\\n\\r\\n- I\'m using the Laserbear 3D printed SD card tray, but have tried without it and it\'s the same problems.\\r\\n\\r\\n- I\'ve tried multiple versions of Tekken 3, mostly Redump.\\r\\n\\r\\n- I\'ve even tried a different PSU, as I had a PicoPS1PSU available - I think that actually made it worse, but either way neither the Pico nor the original PSU stopped the skipping.\\r\\n\\r\\nTrying to think of anything else - basically I\'ve tried everything I can reasonably think of, and nothing\'s helping. Games work, the HDMI output works, it\'s just this skipping problem cropping up.\\r\\n\\r\\nI\'ve also seen some green artifacts\\/glitches on screen sometimes (they\'re in the videos linked above), though only when using 960p mode OR when using passthru on the PS1Digital. Aware that makes that not an XStation issue, just something to mention here for the sake of it.","comments":"0","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues\\/issues\\/51\\/comments","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:22Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues\\/issues\\/51\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues\\/issues\\/51","id":"777488311","labels":[],"labels_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues\\/issues\\/51\\/labels{\\/name}","locked":false,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU3Nzc0ODgzMTE=","number":"51","repository_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues","state":"open","title":"FMV skipping most - not all - of the time (also audio)","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:22Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/x-station\\/xstation-issues\\/issues\\/51","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars3.git