{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/826111?","display_login":"jayunit100","gravatar_id":"","id":"826111","login":"jayunit100","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100"},"created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:28Z","id":"14690758208","org":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/13629408?","gravatar_id":"","id":"13629408","login":"kubernetes","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/orgs\\/kubernetes"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"author_association":"MEMBER","body":"Ok, makes sense. So the definition of conformance for a mixed OS cluster ... is going to be that the \\"OS specific\\" conformance tests pass, and the Linux ones pass as well?  \\n\\n","created_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:28Z","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/96639#issuecomment-753495878","id":"753495878","issue_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/96639","node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc1MzQ5NTg3OA==","updated_at":"2021-01-02T16:40:28Z","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/comments\\/753495878","user":{"avatar_url":"https:\\/\\/avatars3.githubusercontent.com\\/u\\/826111?v=4","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/events{\\/privacy}","followers_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/followers","following_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/following{\\/other_user}","gists_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/gists{\\/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/jayunit100","id":"826111","login":"jayunit100","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyNjExMQ==","organizations_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/orgs","received_events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/received_events","repos_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/starred{\\/owner}{\\/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100\\/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/users\\/jayunit100"}},"issue":{"assignees":[],"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"As Kubernetes on Windows continues to grow, there is a growing need to be able to define Conformance for clusters containing Windows Nodes.\\r\\n\\r\\n### Current conformance definition & process\\r\\n\\r\\nDetails: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/cncf\\/k8s-conformance\\r\\n\\r\\n> All vendors are invited to submit conformance testing results for review and certification by the CNCF, which formally certifies conformant implementations.\\r\\n\\r\\n> This program gives end users the confidence that when they use a Certified Kubernetes product they can rely on a high level of common functionality. It gives Independent Software Vendors (ISVs) confidence that if their customer is using a Certified Kubernetes platform that their software will behave as expected.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe current process to have a certified **conformant** distribution:\\r\\n\\r\\n- https:\\/\\/github.com\\/cncf\\/k8s-conformance\\/blob\\/master\\/instructions.md\\r\\n- Summary: tests are run via Sonobuy & submitted via PR to the cncf\\/k8s-conformance repo in a specific format described in docs.\\r\\n\\r\\nGoldenList of all conformance tests: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/blob\\/master\\/test\\/conformance\\/testdata\\/conformance.yaml\\r\\n\\r\\nIs this a goal?\\r\\n\\r\\n#### NodeConformance vs Conformance\\r\\n\\r\\nCurrently there is no exact definition on what NodeConformance means. An ongoing discussion can be found [here](https:\\/\\/github.com\\/kubernetes\\/test-infra\\/issues\\/18973) and [here](https:\\/\\/docs.google.com\\/document\\/d\\/1Ne57gvidMEWXR70OxxnRkYquAoMpt56o75oZtg-OeBg\\/edit), in the sig-node meeting notes.\\r\\n\\r\\nHighlights of discussion: \\r\\n> **Tests tagged with NodeConformance were intended to include sig-node e2e tests agnostic of cloud providers, OS distributions and container runtimes and expected to pass for every PR**\\r\\n\\r\\n> **Today, the NodeConformance tag is rarely added to new tests and details on it can only be found here in the documentation. One test was added July 8th, 2020, and prior to that, November 6th, 2019 was the last time it was added.**\\r\\n\\r\\nAs well, there is no current process by which you describe a node as conformant.\\r\\nThere is no process by which one test gets promoted to NodeConformance ( However, there is a Conformance promotion process ).\\r\\n\\r\\nOpen questions:\\r\\n- Does the fact that a cluster containing Windows Nodes pass all NodeConformance tagged tests make it Conformant?\\r\\n\\r\\n##### State of e2e tests covering a K8s Node:\\r\\n\\r\\n- There are 145 tagged NodeConformance tests in e2e suite, out of which only 98 can run on Windows.\\r\\n\\r\\n- There is overlap in Conformance & NodeConformance tests:\\r\\n    - 89 tests are marked both Conformance & NodeConformance. \\r\\n\\r\\n- There are 28 separate tests marked sig-windows, that test Windows specific features ( GMSA ) or attempt to replace NodeConformance tests marked ( LinuxOnly ).\\r\\n\\r\\n##### What does conformance mean for a Windows Node \\/ Cluster Containing Windows nodes?\\r\\n\\r\\n- Pass Conformance & NodeConformance tagged tests ( except LinuxOnly )\\r\\n- Pass sig-windows tagged tests?\\r\\n\\t- some sig-windows tests are testing specific features like GMSA, this most likely shouldn\'t be part of a Windows Conformance suite.\\r\\n- CNI: does passing all sig-networking tagged tests from the Conformance suite make the node conformant? Are there specific tests to cover for Windows?\\r\\n- Isolation Mode: Process vs HyperV Containers.\\r\\n\\t- Can we have both at the same time in a cluster?\\r\\n- Hybrid Clusters: ?\\r\\n- CSI: ?\\r\\n- Future Features: Privileged Containers, LCOW\\r\\n\\r\\nRelated: https:\\/\\/github.com\\/kubernetes\\/enhancements\\/issues\\/1618","comments":"6","comments_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/96639\\/comments","created_at":"2020-11-17T15:33:47Z","events_url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/96639\\/events","html_url":"https:\\/\\/github.com\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/issues\\/96639","id":"744844002","labels":[{"color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":"Issues or PRs related to kubernetes conformance tests","id":"717986501","name":"area\\/conformance","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MTc5ODY1MDE=","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/labels\\/area\\/conformance"},{"color":"0052cc","default":false,"id":"105152717","name":"area\\/test","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMDUxNTI3MTc=","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/labels\\/area\\/test"},{"color":"c7def8","default":false,"description":"Categorizes issue or PR as related to a new feature.","id":"267761362","name":"kind\\/feature","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjc3NjEzNjI=","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/labels\\/kind\\/feature"},{"color":"ededed","default":false,"description":"Indicates an issue or PR lacks a `triage\\/foo` label and requires one.","id":"2389815605","name":"needs-triage","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMzg5ODE1NjA1","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/labels\\/needs-triage"},{"color":"d2b48c","default":false,"description":"Categorizes an issue or PR as relevant to SIG Architecture.","id":"636152047","name":"sig\\/architecture","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2MzYxNTIwNDc=","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repos\\/kubernetes\\/kubernetes\\/labels\\/sig\\/architecture"},{"color":"d2b48c","default":false,"description":"Categorizes an issue or PR as relevant to SIG Testing.","id":"483069764","name":"sig\\/testing","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0ODMwNjk3NjQ=","url":"https:\\/\\/api.github.com\\/repo